    11| *      (creating + confirming them if they do not exist yet).
    12| *   3. PRESERVES the owner's password: mints the session with a server-side
    13| *      magic-link token (admin generateLink + verifyOtp token_hash). The
    14| *      owner's manual password is NEVER modified by this flow anymore.
    15| *      (The previous behavior reset the password on every call, which kept
    16| *      breaking the owner's manual email+password sign-in.)
    17| *   4. Falls back to the legacy password self-heal ONLY if the magic-link
    18| *      session mint fails, so owner access can never be fully locked out.
    19| *
    20| * No password is ever sent back to the client. The client installs the
    21| * returned session via supabase.auth.setSession(), which produces a real
    22| * Supabase session — so owner-AI chat approval (allowlist + bearer check)
